  'scale-stock-query-shape.test.mjs', // §27DF: the stock-list QUERY SHAPE that a small tenant cannot distinguish — the availability merge must publish four scalars (never `$$ROOT`) and hydrate the page afterwards, both paged catalog aggregates must opt into `allowDiskUse`, `outOfStock` must stay row-local (no per-row product join) and `lowStock` must prefilter against the tenant's largest `minimumStock` above the join — written after the 131 000-product tenant crossed MongoDB's 100 MB `$group` limit and failed four assistant tools and the products low-stock list, with an in-memory positive control per checker proving each one can fail
  'OPS2-operational-counters.test.mjs', // OPS-2: the pulse an outside watcher can read — unit: the status classification (and `other` for anything that is not a status at all), the accumulation rule that a 4xx is not a server error, the snapshot being a copy a caller cannot use to make itself look healthy, the fixed published surface with no path/id/message/duration in it, the bounded per-status map under 100 distinct 5xx codes, and the source guard that the counter is installed BEFORE the first route; db: over the real app — a finished request is counted, a 404 lands in 4xx and leaves the error count alone, `/live` and `/ready` stay exactly what they were (no counters key at all), and a REAL 503 from a dropped database connection is counted with its timestamp, which is the reading that was invisible while five assistant tools were failing and `/ready` reported ready
  'AI15-location-name.test.mjs', // AI-15: the location a member named, without a provider round-trip to translate it — `getInventory`/`getProductsByLocation` accept an exact `location` name as well as an id, the name path returns the SAME rows as the id path, case/whitespace are forgiven but a description fragment is not, only ACTIVE locations of the session's own business resolve, a duplicated name returns BOTH candidates rather than picking one, asking by both forms is refused, and neither form is refused politely instead of listing the whole catalogue
